## PART II — Match Day: The Critical Pre-Match Window

**3–4 Hours Before Kick-Off — Primary Glycogen-Loading Meal**
- Carbs: 2 g/kg (~150 g for 75 kg player) · Protein: 20–30 g lean · Fat <10 g · Fibre <5 g
- Example: 200g white rice + 150g grilled chicken + 100g carrots + banana + electrolyte water
- Example: 200g pasta, tomato sauce (no oil), lean white fish, white bread roll
- *Evidence:* 2 g/kg CHO at 3–4h improves time to fatigue and intermittent running (Sherman et al., 1991; Thomas et al., 2016); low fat/fibre speeds gastric emptying, cuts GI complaints (de Oliveira et al., 2014)

**~60 Minutes Before — Optional Top-Up Only**
- ≤30 g rapid carbs, only foods tested in training: banana, toast + honey, low-fibre bar, or 150–200ml sports drink
- *Evidence:* >50g high-GI carbs pre-exercise risks rebound hypoglycaemia in unadapted individuals (Foster et al., 1979); ≤30g minimizes this

**Warm-Up — 4-Pillar Sequence**
1. Dynamic mobility (5 min): lunges, leg swings, hip circles, thoracic rotation
2. Movement prep (5 min): jog, high knees, butt kicks, shuffle, carioca
3. Neuromuscular potentiation (5 min): 10–30m sprints, vertical jumps, reactive COD
4. Mental blueprinting (3 min): tactical visualization, box-breathing (4-4-4), communication cues

