## PART VIII — Daily Monitoring & Decision Heuristics

Track each morning: sleep duration/quality, resting HR & HRV, hydrated body mass, urine colour, soreness (0–10), RPE wellness score, GPS training/match load

**Decision matrix**

| Scenario | Interpretation | Action |
|---|---|---|
| High soreness + normal HRV | Likely neural/perceptual | Active recovery, soft-tissue work, no load reduction |
| High soreness + HRV drop >10% | Physiological strain | Cut intensity (rest day or low bike), raise protein to 2.5 g/kg |
| Low soreness + HRV suppressed | Early fatigue/illness sign | Light aerobic only, medical consult, screen for URS symptoms |
| Normal metrics + subjective tiredness | Psychological/nutritional | Review sleep + carb intake, mental-freshness protocol |
| Body mass loss >1.5% + thirst | Under-recovered fluid deficit | Aggressive rehydration (150% deficit) before next session |

This turns monitoring into a functional recovery operating system rather than single-metric guesswork.

