Appendix C: Glossary of Key Terms

· HRV (Heart Rate Variability): The variation in time intervals between heartbeats, reflecting autonomic nervous system balance. Higher HRV generally indicates better recovery status.
· RPE (Rating of Perceived Exertion): A subjective scale (0–10 or 6–20) used to quantify how hard a session feels.
· Glycogen Supercompensation: A nutritional strategy that increases muscle glycogen stores above normal resting levels through high carbohydrate intake and tapered training.
· Casein: A slow-digesting milk protein that forms a gel in the stomach, providing a sustained release of amino acids; ideal for overnight recovery.
· MPS (Muscle Protein Synthesis): The metabolic process of building new muscle proteins, critical for repair and adaptation.
· EPOC (Excess Post-Exercise Oxygen Consumption): The elevated oxygen consumption above resting levels after exercise, reflective of metabolic cost of recovery.
· DOMS (Delayed Onset Muscle Soreness): Muscle pain and stiffness felt 24–72 hours after unaccustomed or high-intensity exercise.
· WBGT (Wet Bulb Globe Temperature): A measure of heat stress that considers temperature, humidity, wind speed, and radiation; used to modify training/match hydration strategies.
· ML (Machine Learning): A subset of artificial intelligence in which algorithms learn patterns from data to make predictions or decisions without explicit programming.

