Recovery Score Calculation (Simplified)
Each variable is normalised against a 28-day rolling baseline. Weightings are initially equal but adjusted by a gradient-boosted model based on injury correlation.
Recovery Score = (HRV z-score × 0.25) + (Sleep quality z-score × 0.20) + (Soreness inverted z-score × 0.20) + (RPE load fatigue index × 0.15) + (Hydration marker z-score × 0.10) + (Nutrition compliance % × 0.10)

Thresholds for Automated Recommendations

· Recovery Score ≥ 85: Green. Full training load permitted.
· 70–84: Amber. Reduce high-speed running volume by 15–20%; retain skill and tactical sessions.
· <70: Red. Do not clear for full training; active recovery or modified session only. Injury-risk alert triggered; staff must review.

Model Retraining Protocol

· Monthly: Compare predicted injury flags (amber/red days) against actual medical injuries. Calculate sensitivity, specificity.
· Retrain ensemble model (Random Forest + XGBoost) on updated squad data to adjust feature weights and injury-risk thresholds.
· Cold-water immersion flag remains user-preference toggled; model does not auto-recommend CWI unless player’s historical recovery score improves significantly with CWI use (N-of-1 analysis).

